# World Quiz Race — game API samples.
# VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, start the app (F5), then click "Send Request" above each block, in order.
# Visual Studio 2026 also runs this file. Cookies (anti-forgery) are kept between requests.

@host = http://localhost:5255

### 1. Anti-forgery token (sets the cookie; the token goes in the X-CSRF-TOKEN header of every POST)
# @name csrf
GET {{host}}/api/game/antiforgery

### 2. Register both players and create the match
# @name create
POST {{host}}/api/game/matches
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "playerA": { "name": "Adam", "age": 9, "avatar": "fox" },
  "playerB": { "name": "Lina", "age": 13, "avatar": "panda" }
}

@matchId = {{create.response.body.$.matchId}}
@playerA = {{create.response.body.$.players[0].player.id}}
@playerB = {{create.response.body.$.players[1].player.id}}

### 3. Match state (positions, routes, checkpoints, whose turn it is)
GET {{host}}/api/game/matches/{{matchId}}

### 4. Current challenge of player A (calling it again returns the same attempt)
# @name challengeA
GET {{host}}/api/game/matches/{{matchId}}/players/{{playerA}}/challenge

### 5. Cheating attempt: player B asks for a challenge during A's turn → 409 not_your_turn
GET {{host}}/api/game/matches/{{matchId}}/players/{{playerB}}/challenge

### 6. Answer of player A. Adapt "answer" to the challenge type (docs/CHALLENGE_FORMATS.md),
###    e.g. {"optionId":"b"}, {"value":12}, {"text":"Paris"}, {"moves":"RDDR"}…
POST {{host}}/api/game/matches/{{matchId}}/answers
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "matchId": {{matchId}},
  "playerChallengeId": {{challengeA.response.body.$.playerChallengeId}},
  "answer": { "optionId": "b" }
}

### 7. Cheating attempt: the same answer replayed (double click) → 409 attempt_already_answered
POST {{host}}/api/game/matches/{{matchId}}/answers
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "matchId": {{matchId}},
  "playerChallengeId": {{challengeA.response.body.$.playerChallengeId}},
  "answer": { "optionId": "b" }
}

### 8. Now it is player B's turn
# @name challengeB
GET {{host}}/api/game/matches/{{matchId}}/players/{{playerB}}/challenge

### 9. Answer of player B
POST {{host}}/api/game/matches/{{matchId}}/answers
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "matchId": {{matchId}},
  "playerChallengeId": {{challengeB.response.body.$.playerChallengeId}},
  "answer": { "value": 0 }
}

### 10. POST without the anti-forgery header → 400
POST {{host}}/api/game/matches
Content-Type: application/json

{ "playerA": { "name": "Eve", "age": 9 }, "playerB": { "name": "Max", "age": 10 } }

### 11. Results (409 match_not_finished until a player reaches the final checkpoint)
GET {{host}}/api/game/matches/{{matchId}}/result
